From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sidey383 <sidey383@mail.ru>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 03:45:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XMine: Add Plugin#onPostUnload and
 Server#getWorldContainerPath

Adds a post-unload phase that runs after the worlds have been saved,
closed and unlocked, for plugins that need to touch the raw world files
on disk (backups, uploads) once nothing else can be writing to them, and
an absolute path to the world container that stays valid that late.

To make the phase usable at all, SimplePluginManager#beginShutdown tells
the JavaPluginLoader to defer tearing down the plugin class loaders while
plugins are being disabled, so onPostUnload can still load classes and
read resources out of the plugin jars; postUnloadPlugins closes them once
no plugin code will run again.

Nothing can interrupt onPostUnload - the watchdog is stopped before the
shutdown sequence starts - so each call is timed and a plugin that runs
over xmine.postUnloadWarnMillis is named in the log.

